{"title":"LinguaLeap","sub":"Weekly users of a language app fell 8%. Why?","type":"Product case","industry":"Consumer tech / education","geo":"Global","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25 min","skills":"Root cause · segmenting before guessing","prompt":"You're a product manager at LinguaLeap, a language-learning app. This morning the dashboard shows weekly active users (WAU) down 8% compared with last week. Your boss asks you to find out why.","clarify":[{"q":"How is WAU measured?","a":"Users who complete at least one lesson in 7 days. Definition unchanged."},{"q":"Sudden or gradual?","a":"Sudden: WAU was stable for months, then dropped over 4-5 days."},{"q":"Seasonality?","a":"No holiday this week; last year the same week was flat."}],"structure":{"root":"Why did WAU fall 8%?","branches":[{"head":"Check the data","items":["Tracking or definition change?","Dashboard bug?"]},{"head":"External","items":["Seasonality, holidays","Competitor launch","App store / OS changes"]},{"head":"Internal","items":["New app release","Experiments","Notifications, outages"]},{"head":"Segment the drop","items":["Platform","Country","New vs existing users","Funnel step"]}]},"hypothesis":"A sudden drop with no season to explain it usually means something we changed. I'd segment by platform and check recent releases first.","questions":[{"q":"Here's WAU by platform. What's going on?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"372.517678pt\" height=\"186.956pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 372.517678 186.956\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 186.956 L 372.517678 186.956 L 372.517678 0 L 0 0 L 0 186.956 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 30.4 161.056 L 365.2 161.056 L 365.2 28 L 30.4 28 L 30.4 161.056 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matp