8 Q 1376 2918 1123 2646 Q 870 2374 870 1933 L 870 1370 Q 870 928 1123 656 Q 1376 384 1805 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" d=\"M 1056 0 L 544 0 L 544 3302 L 1056 3302 L 1056 2694 L 1088 2694 Q 1146 2854 1267 2992 Q 1389 3130 1581 3216 Q 1773 3302 2042 3302 L 2240 3302 L 2240 2790 L 1939 2790 Q 1664 2790 1465 2716 Q 1267 2643 1161 2521 Q 1056 2400 1056 2240 L 1056 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" d=\"M 1792 -77 Q 1350 -77 1014 137 Q 678 352 489 739 Q 301 1126 301 1651 Q 301 2176 489 2563 Q 678 2950 1014 3164 Q 1350 3379 1792 3379 Q 2234 3379 2570 3164 Q 2906 2950 3094 2563 Q 3283 2176 3283 1651 Q 3283 1126 3094 739 Q 2906 352 2570 137 Q 2234 -77 1792 -77 z\nM 1792 378 Q 2208 378 2470 634 Q 2733 890 2733 1414 L 2733 1888 Q 2733 2413 2470 2669 Q 2208 2925 1792 2925 Q 1382 2925 1116 2669 Q 851 2413 851 1888 L 851 1414 Q 851 890 1116 634 Q 1382 378 1792 378 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-1e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" transform=\"translate(64.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5\" transform=\"translate(120.890625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(178.890625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(215.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(271.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5\" transform=\"translate(296.09375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p0b4457fc43\"><rect x=\"30.4\" y=\"28\" width=\"334.8\" height=\"133.056\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · WAU index by platform (Week −4 = 100)","note":"Android app version 5.2 was released at the start of this week. Android = ~45% of users. Index values: iOS stays at 100–101; Android is 99–100 until this week, then 82."},"answer":"<p>iOS is flat. <b>Android fell ~18%</b> (45% of users × 18% ≈ 8% overall ✓). It started the same week as Android release 5.2. <b>So-what:</b> almost certainly caused by the release, not by users or competitors.</p>"},{"q":"What would you check next?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Crash rate and app-start success on 5.2</li> <li><b>Push notification delivery</b>: lesson reminders bring back many users; a change in permissions could silently stop them</li> <li>Funnel: open app → start lesson → finish lesson, to see where Android users drop</li></ul> <p><i>Interviewer reveals:</i> reminder notifications delivered on Android fell from 92% to 15% after 5.2, because a new permission prompt is declined by most users.</p>"},{"q":"What do you do now?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Now:</b> hotfix that asks for the permission at a better moment, with a clear explanation (e.g. after the user's first lesson streak)</li> <li><b>Recover:</b> email/in-app message to affected users to switch reminders back on</li> <li><b>Prevent:</b> add 'notifications delivered' to release checklists and alerts</li></ul>"}],"reco":"The 8% drop is an Android problem caused by release 5.2: a new notification permission is being declined, so reminders no longer reach most users and fewer come back for lessons. Ship a hotfix that asks for the permission at a better moment, win back affected users by email, and add notification delivery to the release checklist so it can't happen silently again.","great":["Checks data and definitions first","Segments before guessing","Confirms the size (45% × 18% ≈ 8%)","Fixes now and prevents it happening again"],"id":15,"slug":"lingualeap"}